{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/170544-rumpelstiltskin","id":170544,"title":"Rumpelstiltskin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-16T04:25:54-07:00","id":170544,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Rumpelstiltskin","content":"I'm certain I remember reading the Rumpelstiltskin story (from the Changeling point of view) in a sourcebook years ago. Does anyone know which book this was from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3311-alex333","user":"alex333","date":". 06-16-2014, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3311-alex333","name":"alex333","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:48:48-07:00","id":171279,"title":"","content":"Lords of Summer had an entitlement called the Goldspinners, which was essentially an organization of Rumpelstiltskins. Beyond that, I can't recall if the actual story came up anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T22:28:54-07:00","id":171422,"title":"","content":"I remember the story having to do with how horrible the girl was for having broke her oath to Rumpelstiltskin. As you can imagine, the Fae would tell the story of an oathbreaker differently than the versions humans tell each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3311-alex333","name":"alex333","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T10:16:42-07:00","id":171746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/170544-rumpelstiltskin?p=171279#post171279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lords of Summer had an entitlement called the Goldspinners, which was essentially an organization of Rumpelstiltskins. Beyond that, I can't recall if the actual story came up anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the goldspinning Rumplestiltskin is closer to being a Pearl Satrap. The Goldspinners are more about long term investments; they give you money and you do something productive with that money.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alex333</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/170544-rumpelstiltskin?p=171422#post171422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the story having to do with how horrible the girl was for having broke her oath to Rumpelstiltskin. As you can imagine, the Fae would tell the story of an oathbreaker differently than the versions humans tell each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely the one from the Guild of Goldspinners.<br /> <br /> And they sure do tell it differently; they blame the girl for agreeing to sell her child in the first place. Which, if you think about it, is a completely justified viewpoint. A parent betraying a child like that is far worse than a faerie buying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:47:13-07:00","id":173460,"title":"","content":"In the opening fiction to <i>Dancers in the Dusk</i>, one of the stories Liane tells the Fae is a twisted version of Rumpelstiltskin, in which the king of the ogres eats him in a rage. Could that be what you are thinking of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}